# Resume Tailor Project

This repo tailors a LaTeX CV from structured YAML based on job descriptions.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `master/resume.yaml` | Canonical CV — edit only via manual changes or `/update-resume` |
| `output/{slug}/resume.yaml` | Tailored variant per job application |
| `output/{slug}/jd-analysis.md` | Full audit report (git tracked) |
| `output/{slug}/{Company}_{Role}_{Date}.pdf` | Generated PDF (gitignored) |
| `docs/projects-catalog.yaml` | GitHub-sourced project metadata for JD matching |
| `docs/tailoring-playbook.md` | ATS rules and rewrite guidelines |
| `scripts/render.py` | YAML → LaTeX |
| `scripts/build.sh` | Docker latexmk PDF build |

## Natural Language Routing

When the user pastes a job description or asks to tailor/customize/update their CV/resume for a specific role:

1. Follow the **tailor-resume** skill (`.agents/skills/tailor-resume/SKILL.md`)
2. Do NOT edit `master/resume.yaml` during tailoring

When the user asks to add experience, bullets, or projects to their master CV:

1. Follow the **update-resume** skill (`.agents/skills/update-resume/SKILL.md`)

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- Education and certifications are **fully static** — never tailored
- Missing JD skills are **reported only** — never added to CV
- Aggressive rewrites must preserve truthful facts and metrics
- Soft 1-page limit: warn in audit, do not auto-trim
- Build PDFs with: `make build-variant SLUG={slug}` or `make build-master`

## Build Commands

```bash
make install-deps      # Python: PyYAML, Jinja2
make docker-build      # One-time Docker LaTeX image
make build-master      # Preview canonical CV PDF
make build-variant SLUG=my-company-role-2026-08-24
make validate          # Validate master YAML schema
```
